From 94d08917f9dda6eae21a30e4ad8932ae86926e0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:58:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 61/88] xhttp: HTTP/3 takes another connection when one is out
 of streams

A server allows so many open streams to a QUIC connection, 100 with quic-go's
defaults, and the HTTP/3 client waits for a free one where the HTTP/2 client
opens another connection. With the three connections of the default XMUX the
sessions past about 300 hung until others ended (lab: 288 of 300 sessions
answered, in packet-up and in stream-one; the Xray client: 300 of 900).

An HTTP/3 pool connection now counts its requests and opens one more QUIC
connection past 90 on each; the added ones close after 30 idle seconds. 900 of
900 sessions in both modes.
